{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The reusable cable straps fit my recent Ethernet cables and desk accessories because they help organize wiring while keeping it easy to change.",
    "The USB drive and conventional wireless mouse support practical tasks in my computer setup: moving files between devices and working comfortably at my desk."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The HDMI cable and touchpad keyboard repeat functions my existing equipment already covers; similarity alone does not give me a reason to replace them.",
    "The 24-port switch exceeds my apparent networking needs, the CPU cooler assumes an upgrade I have not planned, and the discontinued UPS would require more investigation before I chose it."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in computer accessories seems to have been stretched into a general interest in hardware upgrades, even when I have no specific need for them.",
    "My headphone and Raspberry Pi purchases seem to suggest more audio equipment and another keyboard, although those purchases already serve those purposes."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases point toward organizing and maintaining a working setup, so useful additions feel more relevant than replacements for equipment I already have.",
    "Scale and immediate usefulness matter: reusable straps suit changing desk wiring, while a large network switch or a different mouse style needs a clearer purpose."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my practical computer interests but sometimes confused useful additions with redundant equipment or unsupported upgrades."
}"}
